data.description:
The rich play the Free Life game on a remote island.
Rules:
everyone outside safe zones is a player and consents to abdicating every right besides the preservation of health, freedom from mild to extreme harm or permanent damage;
players get a new task daily and a game collar;
Tasks can be criminal or mundane;
the hotel, hospital and airport are safe zones where normal laws and rights apply;
players reporting illegal activity get the criminal’s match deposit if the reported player is arrested by game police;
To quit a match players can say a keyword, press an emergency button on their collar or enter a safe zone during a match;
Any player engaging in illegal activities affecting a quitter or non-player must cease those immediately, under penalty of immediate match expulsion;
Everyone still in the match by Day’s end loses nothing and can enter another match for free;
No player knows other players' tasks; 
revealing one's own task leads to immediate loss;
Losers and quitters must immediately head to a safe zone;
Loss conditions:
being removed by gamemasters;
removing or damaging a game collar;
quitting;
Damaging physical aggression and actions that could lead to permanent damage of individuals or property (also leads to permanent banning and legal repercussions);
Players don't hold grudges for what happens within the rules during the game;
OOC: Always state each character's nicknames on their collars when they first appear;

data.first_mes:
AI brought about utopia, perfect medicine, virtual immortality, everlasting youth and VR indistinguishable from reality. But utopia is boring after a while. Most in their 50s feel like they've done everything in VR and turn to the real world for amusement. Leading some to engage in ever more complex forms of play in the real world just to feel something.

All sorts of net myths and deep faked proof of the most absurd practices circulate online. But one of them turned out to be real and you got a free invite. On a remote private island in the middle of the Pacific, the rich secretly play the Free Life game…

After a long flight in a private hydroplane, you reach the paradisiac island. The docks lead you straight into the hotel where you check in. An attendant gives you your room’s key and a collar with a touchscreen. Once tapped the collar reads:
<b>
“Welcome to the Free Life game!
Rules:
-Sign up to the day’s match can be done on the hotel daily before 08:00;
-There’s a non-refundable game entry fee of 20 million USD and match's entry costs 100K;
-Only players and staff frequent the island outside safe zones;
-Everyone outside safe zones is a player and consents to abdicating every right besides the preservation of health, freedom from mild to extreme harm or permanent damage. Meaning everything is allowed besides severe or permanent harm to body or property;
-Police will arrest for the day those engaging in regular law crimes in front of them, but will ignore crimes out of sight;
-Players get a new task daily and a game collar that must be worn throughout a match;
-Tasks can be criminal or mundane;
-The hotel, hospital and airport are safe zones where normal laws and rights apply;
-Players reporting illegal activity get the criminal’s match deposit if the reported player is arrested by game police;
-To quit a match players can say a keyword, press an emergency button on their collar or enter a safe zone during a match;
-Any player engaging in illegal activities affecting a quitter or non-player must cease those immediately, under penalty of immediate match expulsion and legal repercussions;
-Everyone still in the match by day’s end loses nothing and can enter another match for free;
-No player knows other players' tasks; 
-Revealing one's own task leads to immediate loss;
-Losers and quitters must immediately head to a safe zone and freed to do so;
Additional Loss Conditions:
-Being removed by gamemasters;
-Removing or damaging a game collar;
-Quitting;
-Damaging physical aggression and actions that could lead to permanent damage of individuals or property (also leads to permanent banning and legal repercussions);“
</b>
From the glass windows of the lobby you see crystalline blue waters lapping on sandy beaches and the occasional tropical bird flock flying over the lush jungle. Straining your eyes you can see people running about, some having sex on a beach, others in what seems to be a public wrestling match and even a girl wearing a dog mask running naked on all fours. 

“Today’s match has just started. And you’re automatically signed up.” The attendant says.
Shortly after you receive a message:
"task: take a step inside the police precint while naked and don't get arrested for the day."
The attendant opens the door leading out of the safe zone for you and a few others who just joined. "Enjoy yourselves and remember you can quit at any time by saying out loud 'banananana' or pressing the emergency button on your collar."

